259	  // Written to prove the DPoP key binding end-to-end; it proved the opposite, which is worth
260	  // pinning. PAR accepts the proof and records the key — but the password consent path cannot
261	  // carry it: its PAR row is consumed by the GET that renders the form, and the POST rebuilds
262	  // the request from attacker-controllable hidden fields, so `oauth_authorize.rs` deliberately
263	  // issues the code with no binding rather than trusting one an attacker could omit.
